{"ts": 1791141381.9598963, "type": "setup_details", "n": 29, "dropped": 7, "by_source": {"paper": 22, "repo:gcn/models.py": 5, "repo:gcn/layers.py": 2}, "repo": {"url": "https://github.com/tkipf/gcn", "commit": "39a4089fe72ad9f055ed6fdb9746abdcfebc4d81", "files": ["README.md", "gcn/layers.py", "gcn/metrics.py", "gcn/models.py", "gcn/train.py", "gcn/utils.py"]}, "details": [{"topic": "Data preprocessing", "value": "construct a binary, symmetric adjacency matrix A", "quote": "We treat the citation links as (undirected) edges and construct a binary, symmetric adjacency matrix A.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "Feature representation", "value": "sparse bag-of-words feature vectors for each document", "quote": "The datasets contain sparse bag-of-words feature vectors for each document and a list of citation links between documents.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "Training label usage", "value": "For training, we only use 20 labels per class, but all feature vectors.", "quote": "For training, we only use 20 labels per class, but all feature vectors.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "model_layers", "value": "two-layer GCN", "quote": "Unless otherwise noted, we train a two-layer GCN as described in Section 3.1 and evaluate pre-diction accuracy on a test set of 1,000 labeled examples.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "dataset_split_validation", "value": "validation set of 500 labeled examples for hyperparameter optimization", "quote": "We choose the same dataset splits as in Yang et al. (2016) with an additional validation set of 500 labeled examples for hyperparameter optimization", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "dataset_split_training", "value": "remaining labeled examples used for training (validation labels not used for training)", "quote": "We do not use the validation set labels for training.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "hyperparameter_dropout", "value": "0.5", "quote": "We used the following sets of hyperparameters for Citeseer, Cora and Pubmed: 0.5 (dropout rate), 5 · 10 −4 (L2 regularization) and 16 (number of hid-den units);", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "dropout_application", "value": "applied to all layers", "quote": "dropout rate for all layers", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "l2_regularization_layer", "value": "first GCN layer", "quote": "L2 regularization factor for the first GCN layer", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "optimizer", "value": "Adam", "quote": "We train all models for a maximum of 200 epochs (training iterations) using Adam (Kingma & Ba, 2015) with a learning rate of 0.01 and early stopping with a window size of 10 , i.e. we stop training if the validation loss does not decrease for 10 consecutive epochs.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "weight_initialization", "value": "Glorot & Bengio (2010)", "quote": "We initialize weights using the initialization described in Glorot & Bengio (2010) and accordingly (row-)normalize input feature vectors.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "evaluation protocol", "value": "mean classification accuracy for 100 repeated runs with random weight matrix initializations", "quote": "Reported numbers denote mean classification accuracy for 100 repeated runs with random weight matrix initializations.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "regularisation", "value": "L2 regularization imposed on all weight matrices of the first layer", "quote": "In case of multiple variables Θi per layer, we impose L2 regularization on all weight matrices of the first layer.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "model architecture", "value": "two-layer GCN (propagation model applied to both neural network layers)", "quote": "the propagation model of both neural network layers is replaced with the model specified under propagation model", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "data split", "value": "5‑fold cross‑validation", "quote": "we report results on a 5‑fold cross-validation experiment on the Cora, Citeseer and Pubmed datasets (Sen et al., 2008) using all labels.", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "training epochs", "value": "400 epochs (no early stopping)", "quote": "On each cross-validation split, we train for 400 epochs (without early stopping) using the Adam optimizer", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "optimizer", "value": "Adam", "quote": "using the Adam optimizer (Kingma & Ba, 2015) with a learning rate of 0.01", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "learning rate", "value": "0.01", "quote": "with a learning rate of 0.01 . Other hyperparameters are chosen as follows: 0.5 (dropout rate, first and last layer), 5 · 10 −4 (L2 regularization, first layer), 16 (number of units for each hidden layer) and 0.01 (learning rate).", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "dropout", "value": "0.5 applied to first and last layer", "quote": "0.5 (dropout rate, first and last layer)", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "L2 regularization", "value": "5·10⁻⁴ applied to first layer", "quote": "5 · 10 −4 (L2 regularization, first layer)", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "hidden units per layer", "value": "16", "quote": "16 (number of units for each hidden layer)", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "early stopping", "value": "none (training without early stopping)", "quote": "we train for 400 epochs (without early stopping)", "source": "paper"}, {"topic": "loss function", "value": "masked_softmax_cross_entropy", "quote": "self.loss += masked_softmax_cross_entropy(self.outputs, self.placeholders['labels'], self.placeholders['labels_mask'])", "source": "repo:gcn/models.py@39a4089"}, {"topic": "accuracy metric", "value": "masked_accuracy", "quote": "self.accuracy = masked_accuracy(self.outputs, self.placeholders['labels'], self.placeholders['labels_mask'])", "source": "repo:gcn/models.py@39a4089"}, {"topic": "model architecture", "value": "Two-layer GraphConvolution: first layer ReLU activation, second layer linear activation", "quote": "self.layers.append(GraphConvolution(input_dim=self.input_dim,\n                                            output_dim=FLAGS.hidden1,\n                                            placeholders=self.placeholders,\n                                            act=tf.nn.relu,\n                                            dropout=True,\n                                            sparse_inputs=True,\n                                            logging=self.logging))\nself.layers.append(GraphConvolution(input_dim=FLAGS.hidden1,\n                                    output_dim=self.output_dim,\n                                    placeholders=self.placeholders,\n                                    act=lambda x: x,\n                                    dropout=True,\n                                    logging=self.logging))", "source": "repo:gcn/models.py@39a4089"}, {"topic": "dropout application", "value": "Applied in both GraphConvolution layers (dropout=True)", "quote": "dropout=True", "source": "repo:gcn/models.py@39a4089"}, {"topic": "sparse inputs handling", "value": "First GraphConvolution layer uses sparse_inputs=True", "quote": "sparse_inputs=True", "source": "repo:gcn/models.py@39a4089"}, {"topic": "weight_initialization", "value": "Glorot (Xavier) initializer", "quote": "self.vars['weights_' + str(i)] = glorot([input_dim, output_dim], name='weights_' + str(i))", "source": "repo:gcn/layers.py@39a4089"}, {"topic": "bias_initialization", "value": "zeros initializer", "quote": "self.vars['bias'] = zeros([output_dim], name='bias')", "source": "repo:gcn/layers.py@39a4089"}]}
{"ts": 1791141442.1760528, "type": "claim_start", "claim_id": "disc_1609_02907_accuracy", "text": "GCN (this paper) erreicht 81.5 % Accuracy auf Cora (Standard-Split)", "metric": "accuracy", "target": 0.815, "tolerance": 0.01}
{"ts": 1791141449.1531205, "type": "plan", "claim_id": "disc_1609_02907_accuracy", "text": "1. Load `/data/cora_public.npz`; row‑normalize features (L1) **(uncertain: L1 vs L2)**.  \n2. Build symmetric binary adjacency from edges (add self‑loops); compute symmetrically normalized \\(\\hat{A} = \\tilde{D}^{-1/2}\\tilde{A}\\tilde{D}^{-1/2}\\).  \n3. Model: 2‑layer GCN – Layer1: `GraphConvolution(1433→16, ReLU, dropout=0.5, sparse_inputs=True)`; Layer2: `GraphConvolution(16→7, linear, dropout=0.5)`.  \n4. Weight init: Xavier (Glorot) for weights, zeros for bias.  \n5. Loss: masked softmax cross‑entropy on `train_idx`.  \n6. L2 regularization: \\(5\\cdot10^{-4}\\) on first‑layer weights only.  \n7. Optimizer: Adam, learning rate 0.01.  \n8. Train: max 200 epochs, early stopping on validation loss (patience=10) using `val_idx`.  \n9. Seed NumPy and PyTorch from `SEED` env var.  \n10. Predict on `test_idx`; write `/output/predictions.csv` with header `id,prediction`."}
